      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm having some trouble with an iam policy for an s3 bucket. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to it but i keep getting an \"access denied\" error in the cloudwatch logs even though i added the s3:PutObject permission. here is the policy i'm using:\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\ncan u take a look and tell me what i'm missing? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, it seems like you're trying to let your Lambda function write logs to an S3 bucket, but the \"access denied\" error is a common issue when the permissions are not quite right. It's a bit like trying to get a group of mischievous goblins to share their treasure map, but they all insist on keeping it to themselves.\n\nFirst, make sure that your Lambda function has the necessary permissions to write logs to CloudWatch. The IAM policy you've provided only allows the Lambda function to put objects into the S3 bucket. You also need to grant it permission to write logs to CloudWatch. Here's an updated policy that should help:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"logs:PutLogEvents\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": [\n        \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*\",\n        \"arn:aws:logs:*:*:log-group:/aws/lambda/my-function:*\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThis policy allows your Lambda function to both put objects into your S3 bucket and write logs",
      "source": "target",
